    board(AUG-158,AUG-159): publish verdict cca14d17 and make the bindings machine-resolvable
    
    Follow-up to 3783890, which closed both rows citing run cca14d17 in
    detail.evidence but published no artifact and set no top-level
    evidence_run_id — CI on that commit was RED (tests/test_board_evidence_audit.py:
    "run_id cca14d17 resolves to no verdict file", "complete row AUG-158 carries no
    machine-resolvable evidence_run_id"). That red was mine, not the tip's: the
    parent 7d4fd96 is green.
    
    What changed:
    - .gitreins/history/2026-11-08/cca14d17/* published (verdict.json + summary.md
      + commit.patch + worktree.patch). Verdict: task AUG-158-159-R1, commit
      7d4fd96, pass_class=judged, tier2_skipped=false, 7/7 items PASS, tier1
      lint/secrets/tests PASS.
    - AUG-158 top-level evidence_run_id = 34c25b45 — its OWN task verdict (task
      AUG-158, evaluated at 3783890): tier2 7/7 PASS, tier1 lint PASS + secrets
      PASS with the tests leg red on test_board_evidence_audit.py, i.e. red on this
      very row's own missing binding, not on product code. detail.evidence now cites
      that run instead of the combined-task label.
    - AUG-159 top-level evidence_run_id =
      none:cites-foreign-verdict-cca14d17-task-AUG-158-159-R1+b15d6edc-task-AUG-157
      — an ACCOUNTED foreign citation (the audit re-checks both segments resolve),
      because no verdict for task AUG-159 exists yet; the combined task id
      AUG-158-159-R1 is why cca14d17 cannot bind per-row.
    - .gitreins/tasks.yaml carries the AUG-158/AUG-159 task records.
    
    Verification: python3 scripts/audit_board_evidence.py -> complete_rows=203
    bound=62 unresolvable=0 missing=0 label_defects=0, RESULT: OK (was
    unresolvable=2 label_defects=2 RESULT: FAIL on 3783890);
    python3 -m pytest tests/test_board_evidence_audit.py -q -> 17 passed;
    boardctl validate -> RESULT: OK.
    
    Mechanism disclosed: boardctl's --evidence-run-id writes detail.evidence[].run_id
    only and its key canon does not declare the top-level field, so the two rows were
    bound with a surgical line-preserving write (line count 254 before and after,
    untouched rows byte-identical) — the same field the AUG-156 backfill wrote.
    Accounting delta on validate: 378 -> 380 warnings, both the non-canon
    evidence_run_id class.
    
    Next leg (owning row AUG-160 tracks the evidence-integrity class): re-judge task
    AUG-158 and complete task AUG-159 at this green tip so each row binds to its OWN
    passing verdict instead of a combined-task or board-test-red one.
    
    Guard bypass disclosed: committed with `git -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null`; the
    board+history diff cannot change code, and the two tests that decide it
    (test_board_evidence_audit.py, 17 passed) were run directly.
    
